---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocMock from '../../../components/DocMock.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'quick-fixes',         text: 'Quick fixes to try first' },
  { id: 'symptom-table',       text: 'Symptom lookup table' },
  { id: 'diagnostics',         text: 'Generating a support report' },
  { id: 'safe-to-spend-wrong', text: 'Safe to Spend looks wrong' },
  { id: 'premium-not-unlocking',text: 'Premium not unlocking' },
  { id: 'date-issues',         text: 'Transaction date issues' },
  { id: 'backup-fails',        text: 'Backup fails' },
  { id: 'notifications',       text: 'Notifications not arriving' },
  { id: 'app-crashes',         text: 'App crashes on launch' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="BudgetBaby troubleshooting: quick fixes, symptom lookup table, how to generate a support report, and per-issue solutions."
  canonical="/budgetbaby/docs/troubleshooting"
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Troubleshooting</h1>
    <p class="docs-summary">
      Most BudgetBaby issues are resolved in a few steps. Start with the quick fixes below,
      then use the symptom table to find your specific issue. If nothing here helps,
      generate a support report and send it to the support team.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Quick checks" caption="Force-quit, update, check iOS, this resolves most reported issues.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span></span><span class="dm-bar-title">Quick fixes</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">1</span><span class="dm-row-label">Force-quit & reopen<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Swipe up · swipe app away</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">2</span><span class="dm-row-label">iOS 17.0 or later<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Settings → General → About</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">3</span><span class="dm-row-label">Update from App Store<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Profile → pull to refresh</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">4</span><span class="dm-row-label">Working internet<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">For backup, sync, restore</div></span></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="quick-fixes">Quick fixes to try first</h2>
    <p>Before diving into specific issues, run through these four checks. They resolve the majority of reported problems.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Force-quit and reopen the app.</strong> Swipe up from the Home bar to enter the app switcher, swipe BudgetBaby off the screen, then reopen it.</li>
      <li><strong>Check your iOS version.</strong> BudgetBaby requires iOS 17.0 or later. Go to Settings → General → About to check. Update if you are on an older version.</li>
      <li><strong>Update the app.</strong> Open the App Store, tap your profile icon, and pull down to check for updates. Many issues are fixed in recent releases.</li>
      <li><strong>Check your internet connection.</strong> Cloud backup, sync, and Premium restore all require a working internet connection.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="symptom-table">Symptom lookup table</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Symptom</th>
            <th>Likely cause</th>
            <th>Fix</th>
            <th>Contact support when</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Safe to Spend shows 0 or a negative number</td>
            <td>Unpaid red (Essentials) bills exceed remaining budget, or income is entered incorrectly</td>
            <td>Mark paid bills as paid; check income in Settings → Budget Settings; tap the info button to see the full breakdown</td>
            <td>Numbers still do not match after following the Safe to Spend steps below</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Transactions appear on the wrong day</td>
            <td>Timezone handling issue fixed in v2.0.5</td>
            <td>Update the app; re-save affected transactions to apply the fix to existing records</td>
            <td>Dates are still wrong after updating to the latest version</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Premium not active after purchase</td>
            <td>App Store cache or wrong Apple ID signed in</td>
            <td>Settings → Premium Features → Restore Purchases; wait 30 seconds; force-quit and reopen</td>
            <td>Restore fails after confirming you are signed in with the purchasing Apple ID</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Cloud backup fails</td>
            <td>Not signed in, no internet, or backup slot full</td>
            <td>Sign in at Settings → Account; check connection; delete existing backup if slot is full</td>
            <td>All steps tried and backup still fails</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Notifications not arriving</td>
            <td>iOS notification permission denied, or wrong days selected</td>
            <td>iOS Settings → BudgetBaby → Notifications → Allow Notifications; check Settings → Reminders</td>
            <td>Permission is enabled, reminders are configured correctly, and notifications still do not arrive</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>App crashes on launch</td>
            <td>App is outdated or data store is corrupted</td>
            <td>Update the app; if it still crashes, restore from a cloud backup, then reinstall</td>
            <td>Before uninstalling if you have no cloud backup, we may be able to help recover data</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Bills not appearing in the current period</td>
            <td>Bill due date falls outside the current period dates</td>
            <td>Check the bill due date and the current period start/end dates in Settings → Budget Settings</td>
            <td>Due date is inside the period and bill still does not appear</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Money pool balance looks wrong</td>
            <td>Starting balance not set, or a transaction was logged with the wrong payment method</td>
            <td>Check Settings → Payment Methods → Money Setup for starting balances; review recent transactions for incorrect payment methods</td>
            <td>Balances are still wrong after reviewing all transactions</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="diagnostics">Generating a support report</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Support & Diagnostics" caption="Three ways to capture state, guided flow recommended for bugs.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Support</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-accent">
          <div class="dm-h2">Report a Problem</div>
          <div class="dm-help">5-step guided flow. Choose an area, pick a time, attach the bundle.</div>
          <div class="dm-btn dm-btn-primary" style="margin-top:4px;">Start Report</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-h2">Export Diagnostics</div>
          <div class="dm-help">One-tap snapshot of current app state.</div>
          <div class="dm-btn dm-btn-secondary" style="margin-top:4px;">Export</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-h2">Copy Support Report</div>
          <div class="dm-help">Plain-text summary to your clipboard.</div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
      <DocMock label="Bundle preview" caption="Anonymous events, device snapshot, counts only, never financial data.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Support</span><span class="dm-bar-title">BB-9F3K-2A17</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Share</span></div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-good" style="text-align:center;">
          <div class="dm-hero-label">Issue fingerprint</div>
          <div class="dm-hero-amount" style="font-size:18px; color:#A78BFA;">BB-9F3K-2A17</div>
          <div class="dm-hero-sub">Generated Mar 01, 14:35</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Events log</span><strong>1,842</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Device</span><strong>iPhone 15 Pro</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>iOS</span><strong>17.4.1</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>App build</span><strong>2.1.3 (412)</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Tx count</span><strong>1,283</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Amounts/desc.</span><strong class="green">Excluded</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">Bundle: BudgetBaby_Diagnostics_…BB-9F3K-2A17.budgetbaby-diagnostics</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <p>
      BudgetBaby has a built-in diagnostics engine that packages everything the support team needs
      to understand what is happening on your device, without ever including your financial data.
      For anything beyond a simple question, attaching a support report speeds up resolution significantly.
    </p>
    <h3>How to generate a report</h3>
    <p>Go to <strong>Settings → Support and Diagnostics</strong>. You have three options:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Report a Problem</strong> (recommended for bugs). Tap "Start Report." The guided 5-step flow asks which area is affected and when the issue occurred. It then generates a full diagnostics bundle and prompts you to send it. Choose an area: Backup, Restore, Bills, Subscriptions, Spending Buckets, Money on Hand, Premium / Paywall, or Other.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Export Diagnostics</strong> (quick, no prompts). One tap creates the bundle immediately. Use this if you want to capture the current app state without going through the guided flow.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Copy Support Report</strong> (for pasting into emails). Copies a plain-text summary to your clipboard. Useful if you are writing from a desktop or want to paste the report inline.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What is in the report</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Events log.</strong> Last 24 hours of app activity, up to 2,000 events. No financial data: only action types, screen names, and outcomes.</li>
      <li><strong>Device snapshot.</strong> iPhone model, iOS version, locale, timezone, and build type (App Store or TestFlight).</li>
      <li><strong>App state.</strong> Version, build number, onboarding status, Premium status, backup count, and last backup/restore dates.</li>
      <li><strong>Data fingerprint.</strong> Entity counts only: how many transactions, categories, bills, periods, and goals. No amounts or descriptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Support story.</strong> A human-readable narrative that summarizes the event timeline and highlights anything unusual.</li>
      <li><strong>Issue fingerprint.</strong> A unique <code>BB-XXXX-XXXX</code> identifier for your report. Include this in your email subject line.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Your financial data is never included.</strong> No transaction amounts, descriptions, account names, balances, budget values, or category names appear in the report. Only anonymous counts and app-state metadata.
    </div>
    <h3>How to send it</h3>
    <p>
      After generating the report, iOS presents a share sheet. The fastest route is Mail.
      BudgetBaby pre-fills the subject line with your support code (<code>BB-XXXX-XXXX</code>)
      and attaches the bundle automatically. Send to
      <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If Mail is not configured, use AirDrop to your Mac and attach the file manually,
      or use Copy Support Report to paste the text summary into your email.
    </p>
    <h3>Report archive</h3>
    <p>
      Every report is saved under Settings → Support and Diagnostics → View Archive.
      Reports are kept for 90 days. You can re-share any archived report without regenerating it.
    </p>
    <p>The bundle filename looks like:</p>
    <div class="doc-formula">BudgetBaby_Diagnostics_2026-03-01_14-35_BB-9F3K-2A17.budgetbaby-diagnostics</div>

    <h2 id="safe-to-spend-wrong">Safe to Spend looks wrong</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Audit checklist" caption="Walk these checks before assuming the math is wrong.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span></span><span class="dm-bar-title">STS audit</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Tap (i) for live breakdown</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;">→</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Period start/end correct</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;">✓</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Red bills marked paid</span><span style="color:#FBBF24; font-size:14px;">!</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Savings allocation</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;">✓</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Income is take-home</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;">✓</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-warn">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Likely cause</strong><span class="dm-pill orange">Bill reserve</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="color:#FDBA74;">$420 reserved across two unpaid red bills.</div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap the info button next to Safe to Spend on the home screen to see the full calculation breakdown with your actual numbers.</li>
      <li>Verify your active budget period dates are correct in Settings → Budget Settings.</li>
      <li>Check that upcoming bills are assigned to the current period and that any paid bills are marked as paid. Unpaid red (Essentials) bills are reserved in the calculation.</li>
      <li>Confirm that your savings allocation percentage in Budget Setup matches your intentions.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      If Safe to Spend is 0 or negative and you do not expect it to be, the most common causes are:
      unpaid red (Essentials) bills that exceed the remaining budget, or an income amount that was entered
      incorrectly during setup.
    </p>

    <h2 id="premium-not-unlocking">Premium not unlocking after purchase</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Restore in flight" caption="Restore Purchases re-pulls the receipt from Apple, never charges again.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Premium</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-accent" style="text-align:center;">
          <div class="dm-ring-wrap" style="margin:8px auto;">
            <div class="dm-ring" style="--p:80%; width:42px; height:42px;"></div>
            <span class="dm-ring-inner" style="font-size:7px;">Verifying</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="text-align:center;">Contacting Apple…</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Last known status</span><strong>Inactive</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>App Store ID</span><strong>insightintriguing@…</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Wait time</span><strong class="muted">~10 sec</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">If "Nothing to restore" appears, confirm the right Apple ID is signed in.</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to Settings → Premium Features → Restore Purchases.</li>
      <li>Wait 30 seconds after tapping Restore, then check again.</li>
      <li>Force-quit and reopen the app.</li>
      <li>Make sure you are signed in to the App Store with the Apple ID that made the purchase. Go to Settings → (your name) → Media and Purchases to verify.</li>
      <li>Contact <a href="/budgetbaby/support">support</a> with your order number if the issue persists.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="date-issues">Transaction date issues</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Re-save to repair" caption="Open and Save any affected transaction to apply timezone normalization.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Cancel</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Edit Transaction</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Save</span></div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-warn">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Pre-2.0.5 record</strong><span class="dm-pill orange">!</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="color:#FDBA74;">Date may be off by one day. Save once to normalize to noon UTC.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Description</span><strong>Trader Joe's</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Amount</span><strong>$42.18</strong></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Date</span><strong>Mar 02 · 12:00 UTC</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-h2" style="font-size:10px;">After save</div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Was</span><span class="red">Mar 01</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Now</span><span class="green">Mar 02</span></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <p>
      BudgetBaby normalizes all transaction dates to noon UTC to prevent timezone-related date shifts
      across time zones. If you see dates that are off by one day:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Update BudgetBaby to the latest version. v2.0.5 and later include this fix.</li>
      <li>Re-save any affected transactions. Opening a transaction and tapping Save applies the timezone normalization to that record.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="backup-fails">Backup fails</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Backup error" caption="Each failure surfaces a specific reason and a one-tap fix.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Backup</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-error">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Backup failed</strong><span class="dm-pill red">Slot full</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="color:#FCA5A5;">Free tier supports 1 backup. Delete the existing one first or upgrade.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Account</span><span class="green">Signed in</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Connection</span><span class="green">Wi-Fi</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Slots used</span><strong class="red">1 / 1</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-btn dm-btn-secondary">Delete existing backup</div>
        <div class="dm-btn dm-btn-primary">Upgrade to 5 slots</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li>Verify you are signed in to your BudgetBaby account at Settings → Account.</li>
      <li>Check your internet connection. Backups require an active connection during upload.</li>
      <li>Free users have 1 backup slot. If it is occupied, delete the existing backup first at Settings → Backup &amp; Restore.</li>
      <li>If errors persist after trying all of the above, contact <a href="/budgetbaby/support">support</a> with your account email address.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="notifications">Notifications not arriving</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="iOS permissions" caption="Confirm Allow Notifications, Banners, Sounds, and that no Focus is blocking.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">BudgetBaby</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Notifications</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Allow Notifications</span><span class="dm-toggle on"></span></div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Alerts</div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Lock Screen</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;">✓</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Banners</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;">✓</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-warn">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Sleep Focus is on</strong><span class="dm-pill orange">!</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="color:#FDBA74;">Add BudgetBaby to its allowed-apps list.</div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li>Open iOS Settings → BudgetBaby → Notifications. Ensure Allow Notifications is turned on.</li>
      <li>In BudgetBaby, go to Settings → Reminders. Verify the reminder days and time are configured as you expect.</li>
      <li>Check that quiet hours are not covering the time when you expect the notification.</li>
      <li>Note: Same-day bill reminders are available on the free tier. Multi-day reminders (3 days before, 1 week before) and subscription reminders require Premium.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="app-crashes">App crashes on launch</h2>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Recovery path" caption="Don't uninstall before contacting support, we may rescue local data.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span></span><span class="dm-bar-title">Crash recovery</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-error" style="text-align:center;">
          <span class="dm-icon danger" style="width:30px; height:30px; margin:0 auto;">!</span>
          <div class="dm-h2" style="margin-top:6px;">App keeps crashing</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">1</span><span class="dm-row-label">Update from App Store</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">2</span><span class="dm-row-label">Restore from cloud backup</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon support">3</span><span class="dm-row-label">Email support before uninstalling<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">support@babyblocks.io</div></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon danger">4</span><span class="dm-row-label">Last resort: uninstall + reinstall<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px; color:#FCA5A5;">Deletes local data</div></span></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
    <p>Crashes on launch are rare and usually caused by an outdated app version or a corrupted local data store.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Update BudgetBaby to the latest version from the App Store.</li>
      <li>If the crash continues after updating and you have a cloud backup, restore from it: sign in on another device or reinstall the app, then restore from Settings → Backup &amp; Restore.</li>
      <li>If you do not have a cloud backup, contact <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a> before uninstalling. Include your iOS version and app version. We may be able to help recover your data.</li>
      <li>As a last resort, uninstall and reinstall the app. This will delete all local data.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
